==Enemy==
Contrary to most other [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]] variants inflicting extremely high damage and DPS, Li'l Zyclone acts more as a barrier to cut off the player's meatshield supply. In order to accomplish this, he sports high health, decent movement speed, one knockback and a long burrow distance, as well as quickly reviving with 100% HP once.

==Strategy==
With 333,333 health, this little guy is very good at his job, cutting off your supply of meatshields by burrowing behind your main group of cats with a crazy burrow distance of 1,250. He isn't a threat alone due to his low damage and range.

The absolute best way to deal with Li'l Zyclone is to either stop his burrow with the regular [[Cat Cannon]] or force him to the surface with the [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast Cannon]]. If that is not possible, you will usually want to burst him down as quickly as possible to prevent the other enemies from abusing the limited meatshields for too long. [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] is the optimal choice, but [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]] and [[Li'l Bird Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Flying Cat]] work too. In an emergency, [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] can be used, but don't spawn him without some thought.

Additionally, Li'l Zyclone's long burrow distance can cause him to go straight up to your base. In this case, [[Welterweight Cat (Rare Cat)|Heavyweight Cat]], [[Piledriver Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Power Piledriver Cat]] and [[Meditation Cat (Special Cat)|Meditation Cat]] are ideal for pushing him off.

Unless a [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killer]] lands the finishing blow, he will respawn with full health one time. If a Zombie Killer unit did not kill him, note that he is only dead for less than 5 seconds so you may or may not get lucky by having your faster units walk through the puddle, but slower units probably won't be able to get past it before he revives. If some of your units don't get past the puddle, just rinse and repeat.

If powerful [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance units]] are owned, especially [[:Category:Anti-Zombie Cats|anti-Zombie]] ones, such as [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Vaulter Cat]], Li'l Zyclone can be used as a stepping stone to kill other threats, such as the [[Cadaver Bear]]s in [[Frontier Shrine (Merciless)/Zombie|Necro Frontier]].

